Now. The thing with the Whirligig is it calculates the difficulty of a derivation, and if I understand right, the mathematics that you put together is what you do to reverse engineer the actual derivation from the known difficulty, but the mathematics for doing so is, I assume, quite novel, even for mathematicians. Is that right? 

